SpiderX overlay patch for ros-controls/gz_ros2_control tag 0.7.15
(commit bfc5845aa7f0250cbc384773dba5c9847d609b95), package directory gz_ros2_control/.

Problem: GazeboSimROS2ControlPlugin::Configure() creates its "gz_ros2_control" node before it
installs the <parameters> files as the context's global arguments. Parameter overrides are fixed
when a node is created, so position_proportional_gain (declared on that node by
GazeboSimSystem::initSim()) always took its default, 0.1, whatever the files said.

Change:
- The plugin node now also receives the <parameters> files as node-local --params-file
  arguments (plugin_node_options()). Remapping rules and the robot_description argument are
  passed as before; the controller manager and the controllers are configured as before.
- The gain is declared by declare_position_proportional_gain(): default 0.1 as upstream; a value
  that is not a finite double greater than 0 is reported and initSim() fails (never clamped or
  replaced). The gain is still read once at start-up.
- Offline gtest test_parameter_loading (no Gazebo).

Apply from the repository root: git apply <this file>
